{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169957-the-giftbox-custom-updated-gifts","id":1169957,"title":"The Giftbox (Custom & Updated Gifts)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-23T10:58:00-08:00","id":1169957,"title":"The Giftbox (Custom & Updated Gifts)","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Much to my surprise, I don't think a thread like this has been made before. In the spirit of the Yule Tide Season, post your custom gifts here. You can find the guidelines for creating new gifts <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-1-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. As iteration is the most important part of tweaking Gifts to be balanced correctly, commentary and suggestions are absolutely allowed, just remember to be constructive. <br /> <br /> I'll start us off with the Gift of Lunacy. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gift of Lunacy (Wolf) </span></b></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Know The Moon-Touched</b> (Cunning)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost</b>: 1 Essence </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dice Pool</b>: Wits + Investigation + Cunning</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Action</b>: Instant</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Uratha can use this Facet to detect if any prey have fallen under the sway of Lunacy within 10 yards per dot of Cunning Renown she possesses. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The Uratha gains the Ban Condition. She feels compelled to howl at the moon and make warding gestures at the sun. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Failure</b>: The Facet fails.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Success</b>: The Uratha becomes aware if prey have rolled a breaking point to resist Lunacy in the last scene or if they are currently under the influence of a Condition caused by Lunacy. The Uratha does not know the result of the breaking point roll or the Condition imposed. If the Uratha uses this information influence the way the prey rationalizes the events that cause Lunacy, she gains a +3 bonus to her dice pool.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: The Uratha knows the outcome of the Lunacy breaking point and/or what Condition was imposed. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Manipulative Lunacy</b> (Glory)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost</b>: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Duration</b>: Permanent</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">When the prey fails a roll to resist Lunacy caused by a werewolf with this Facet, open one of the prey's doors. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Lunatic Fringe </b>(Honour)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost</b>: 1 Essence per packmate affected (minimum 1 Essence) </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Action</b>: Instant </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Duration</b>: 1 scene</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">All packmates targeted by this Facet gain 8-again on rolls against characters affected by a Lunacy-imposed Condition. This Facet does not apply to attack rolls or damage-dealing rolls.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Lunar Tidings</b> (Purity)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost</b>: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Duration</b>: Permanent</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">When an Uratha with this Facet cause prey to suffer a Lunacy breaking point, the prey's roll is penalized by the Uratha's dots in Purity Renown. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Light of the Moon</b> (Wisdom)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost</b>: Varies </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Uratha gain Influence (Lunacy) equal to her dots in Wisdom. She can use this Influence in the same way as a spirit. Her dice pool for Influence (Lunacy) is Presence + Intimidate + Wisdom.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> I do have some commentary on this gift, but I will have to save it for later. Thoughts? </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 12-23-2017, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T12:21:49-08:00","id":1169976,"title":"","content":"The Cunning one seems tricky to work out the utility of, in most cases. It does have its niche, though. Same with the Glory and Honor Facets. Purity's is just mean, and the Wisdom Facet is where the real sexiness happens. But then, Influences are always fun to play with. <hr /><br /> <i><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gift of Giving (Shadow)</span></b></i><br /> <br /> <b>Anonymous Donor (Cunning)<br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence per Size of the item<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Dexterity + Larceny + Cunning - Wits + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> The Uratha can send small items through gaps in space, placing them up to Cunning * 5 yards away. You do not need line of sight to the target or location, but if you lack visibility you must know the precise location you are sending the object to. If possession of the item would be unwelcome (such as contraband or a primed grenade), the target reflexively resists it with Wits + Primal Urge (or equivalent).<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Who needs chimneys when you can 'port it through space? Though I did think about sending it through the Gauntlet, and referencing the Gauntlet Strength. Technically this is meant for objects, but if your ST wants to allow it, you could for 5 Essence:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://media.tenor.com/images/81799478a08c856f3c30c3bb39783efa/tenor.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div> ]<br /> <br /> <b>Impressive Generosity (Glory)</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2 Essence<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive<br /> The werewolf can give another a gift of such impressive nature that allies are heartened and enemies are shamed. When bestowing a gift upon another worth at least Resources 1 (relative to the receiver), provided the recipient accepts it, the Uratha can grant or impose one of the following Conditions on Glory + the Resources value of the gift to enemies or allies (whichever received it) - Confused, Guilty, Inspired, Leveraged, or Steadfast.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Still unsure of what to do here. I made it Condition flexible to offer the greatest options, but it seems... bland for that.]<br /> <br /> <b>Obligation (Honor)</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 4 Essence<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive<br /> The Uratha can lace a physical gift with an implicit condition of behavior. The target object is infused with Essence such that anyone claiming ownership of it must accept a Ban (devised by the user of this Gift). The Ban Condition lasts for one lunar month.<br /> <b>Special</b>: If the werewolf spends a point of Willpower, the Ban lasts as long as the recipient possesses or owns the item - the Conditions resolves only if the item is given to (and accepted) by someone else. If they spend a Willpower <b>dot</b>, then the Ban applies to whoever owns the item, affecting any new owners as if they were the original recipient.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Cost is equal to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Law_of_obligations\" target=\"_blank\">elements of obligation</a>? Maybe make the optional cost a dot, since it is permanent? You <i>are</i> making the thing into a &quot;cursed&quot; item, basically.]<br /> <br /> <b>Boon of Power (Purity)</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 to 5 Essence<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> The werewolf can temporarily bestow a portion of their spiritual might upon another willing recipient. Select 1 Gift Facet - the target character gains the Facet and the amount of Essence spent upon activation. They use your Renown in place of their own (if any), and spend only the Essence given to them via this Gift's activation. If the Facet is a permanent effect, the recipient can activate it for 1 Scene for the cost of 1 Essence.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: For as long as the Gift Facet is held by another, you lose access to it. You can cancel the effects of this Gift with an Instant action, provided you have line of sight with the recipient.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: This is more useful when bestowed upon Wolf-Blooded and mortal Pack members, but it can be a nice boon for even other Werewolves in a pinch. The limited Essence investiture gives the effect a shelf life, and the Facet lockout prevents you from spamming the gift. Though considering the Essence cost, that could be eliminate or reduced to a penalty.]<br /> <br /> <b>Heart's Hunger (Wisdom)</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Manipulation + Empathy + Wisdom - Composure + Primal Urge<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Roll Result</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The prey intuits what the werewolf is doing. In addition, the scents are misinterpreted to give a <i>wrong</i> Aspiration.<br /> <b>Failure</b>: A tangled mess of smells obscures the nature of their wants. The Storyteller might give one or two words from an Aspiration.<br /> <b>Success</b>: The Uratha smells the hidden yearnings of the target's heart. For each dot of Wisdom, reveal one of the target's Aspirations. Short term Aspirations are uncovered before long term ones.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: In addition to uncovering the target's Aspirations, the werewolf gains the Informed Condition regarding the target's desires.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: A shameless version of the Embed Heart's Desire. It doesn't uncover Virtue or Vice, but it does give the Informed Condition on ES.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-03-2018, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T13:28:36-08:00","id":1169995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169957-the-giftbox-custom-updated-gifts?p=1169976#post1169976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cunning one seems tricky to work out the utility of, in most cases. It does have its niche, though. Same with the Glory and Honor Facets. Purity's is just mean, and the Wisdom Facet is where the real sexiness happens. But then, Influences are always fun to play with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I didn't want to overshoot the power level, so I errored on the side of weaker. I like them though. Cunning can be used to indirectly track other Uratha indirectly by the Lunacy they cause or intentionally cause Lunacy, then manipulate their memories. Glory can similarly be used to weaponize Lunacy. Would it be too powerful to open a number of doors equal to dots in Glory? Honour should be flexible as long as Lunacy is inflicted. <br /> <br /> Anyhow, here is another gift. It is very much based on Gift of the Elements, but the Influences it grants are sufficiently different that I think they should both coexist reasonably. Also, it clearly demonstrates how much I love mixing Science and Sci-Fi elements into my fantasy horror. <br /> <br /> <u><b>Gift of Radiation</b></u><b> (Shadow)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Heat's Caress</b> (Cunning)<br /> The Uratha gains Influence (Infrared Radiation) equal to her dots in Cunning. She can use this Influence in the same way as a spirit. Her dice pool for Influence (Infrared Radiation) is Dexterity + Survival + Cunning.<br /> <br /> <b>Spread Radiation</b> (Glory) <br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5 Essence per level Influence being used<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Occult + Presence + Glory <br /> <b>Action</b>: Extended (15 success; each roll represents 1 hour)<br /> <br /> This Facet is used in conjunction with the Influence granted by another Radiation Facet, making it operate on a catastrophic scale. An Uratha who posses this Facet is also unaffected by the effects of Influence that other Uratha have augmented with Spread Radiation.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The Uratha suffers the Essence Overloaded Condition. <br /> <b>Failure</b>: No successes are gained, and the Uratha suffers the Stumbled Condition.<br /> <b>Success</b>: Successes are gained. If the target number of successes is hit, the Influence is unleashed on a massive scale, affecting an area of a radius in miles equal to twice the Uratha's Glory Renown. Even minor manifestations of radiation on this scale can be catastrophic, causing mass blackouts, jamming communications, or causing widespread radiation poisoning.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: The Uratha is infused with the power of the electromagnetic spectrum. She may use any of her Radiation Facets' Influences at no cost in Essence for the next day, although further uses of Spread Radiation still cost Essence as normal. <br /> <br /> <b>Flower's Path</b> (Honour) <br /> The Uratha gains Influence (Ultraviolet Radiation) equal to her dots in Honour. She can use this Influence in the same way as a spirit. Her dice pool for Influence (Ultraviolet Radiation) is Socialize + Presence + Honour.<br /> <br /> <b>Nuclear Blessing</b> (Purity) <br /> The Uratha gains Influence (Ionizing Radiation) equal to her dots in Cunning. She can use this Influence in the same way as a spirit. Her dice pool for Influence (Ionizing Radiation) is Intelligence + Science + Purity.<br /> <br /> <b>Heart of Deep Space</b> (Wisdom) <br /> The Uratha gains Influence (Radio Waves) equal to her dots in Wisdom. She can use this Influence in the same way as a spirit. Her dice pool for Influence (Wisdom) is Wits + Investigation + Wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 12-23-2017, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T14:29:13-08:00","id":1170012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169957-the-giftbox-custom-updated-gifts?p=1169995#post1169995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I didn't want to overshoot the power level, so I errored on the side of weaker. I like them though. Cunning can be used to indirectly track other Uratha indirectly by the Lunacy they cause or intentionally cause Lunacy, then manipulate their memories. Glory can similarly be used to weaponize Lunacy. Would it be too powerful to open a number of doors equal to dots in Glory? Honour should be flexible as long as Lunacy is inflicted.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, here is another gift. It is very much based on Gift of the Elements, but the Influences it grants are sufficiently different that I think they should both coexist reasonably. Also, it clearly demonstrates how much I love mixing Science and Sci-Fi elements into my fantasy horror.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Gift of Radiation</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Heat's Caress</b> (Cunning)<br /> The Uratha gains Influence (Infrared Radiation) equal to her dots in Cunning. She can use this Influence in the same way as a spirit. Her dice pool for Influence (Infrared Radiation) is Dexterity + Survival + Cunning.<br /> <br /> <b>Spread Radiation</b> (Glory)<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5 Essence per level Influence being used<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Occult + Presence + Glory<br /> <b>Action</b>: Extended (15 success; each roll represents 1 hour)<br /> <br /> This Facet is used in conjunction with the Influence granted by another Radiation Facet, making it operate on a catastrophic scale. An Uratha who posses this Facet is also unaffected by the effects of Influence that other Uratha have augmented with Spread Radiation.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The Uratha suffers the Essence Overloaded Condition.<br /> <b>Failure</b>: No successes are gained, and the Uratha suffers the Stumbled Condition.<br /> <b>Success</b>: Successes are gained. If the target number of successes is hit, the Influence is unleashed on a massive scale, affecting an area of a radius in miles equal to twice the Uratha's Glory Renown. Even minor manifestations of radiation on this scale can be catastrophic, causing mass blackouts, jamming communications, or causing widespread radiation poisoning.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: The Uratha is infused with the power of the electromagnetic spectrum. She may use any of her Radiation Facets' Influences at no cost in Essence for the next day, although further uses of Spread Radiation still cost Essence as normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Flower's Path</b> (Honour)<br /> The Uratha gains Influence (Ultraviolet Radiation) equal to her dots in Honour. She can use this Influence in the same way as a spirit. Her dice pool for Influence (Ultraviolet Radiation) is Socialize + Presence + Honour.<br /> <br /> <b>Nuclear Blessing</b> (Purity)<br /> The Uratha gains Influence (Ionizing Radiation) equal to her dots in Cunning. She can use this Influence in the same way as a spirit. Her dice pool for Influence (Ionizing Radiation) is Intelligence + Science + Purity.<br /> <br /> <b>Heart of Deep Space</b> (Wisdom)<br /> The Uratha gains Influence (Radio Waves) equal to her dots in Wisdom. She can use this Influence in the same way as a spirit. Her dice pool for Influence (Wisdom) is Wits + Investigation + Wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I &lt;3 Nuclear Power. I feel like it should almost have one Facet called Silent Spring.<br /> <br /> Any feedback on my stubs? I'm trying to work out the exact mechanics (and names).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T14:34:04-08:00","id":1170017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169957-the-giftbox-custom-updated-gifts?p=1170012#post1170012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I &lt;3 Nuclear Power. I feel like it should almost have one Facet called Silent Spring.<br /> <br /> Any feedback on my stubs? I'm trying to work out the exact mechanics (and names).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like you ideas, but I don't know how to execute the mechanics off the top of my head. They seem like they would be fun to play with though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"htt